# Overlay scrollbar: size it for a 3x-zoomed phone and stop it blinking.
# Merged from: webkit-adwaita-scrollbar-scale-env,
# webkit-scrollbar-sprite-and-smoothing, webkit-scrollbar-no-hover-expand.
#
# Atlantic's 3x UI scale is page zoom, which the native scrollbar widget
# ignores, so the Adwaita overlay thumb painted 3 physical px wide on a 1080px
# screen. WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SCALE (1..8, default 1 = upstream) scales the
# metrics; runtime-common.sh sets 3 to match the browser zoom factor.
#
# WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SPRITE=1 paints the thumb once (CPU raster) and moves it via
# setContentsRect instead of Ganesh-repainting a pooled GL texture per scroll
# tick — those repaints are unordered on this driver, which is what produced
# stale/blank thumb frames. WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SMOOTHING low-pass filters the
# displayed position. WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_NO_HOVER=1 keeps the bar in its idle thin
# form (no hover/press expansion into the fat desktop bar + trough when touched),
# which also keeps the sprite fast path — it requires NoPart — active during
# drags.
#
# ---
